# A product whose operand's alternatives include a negative literal (#147):
# {a: -1, b: -9223372036854775808} gives 9223372036854775808, outside int64.
# The target accepts anything, so only the int64 check can refute it, and it
# needs the operand's bounds read from the literal.
-- source.cue --
a: -1 | 0
b: int64
-- target.cue --
m: _
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {m: v0_0.a * v0_0.b}
-- out --
not total
v1_0.m computes v0_0.a * v0_0.b, whose result may be [-9223372036854775807, 9223372036854775808], outside int64; bound the fields it reads so that the result fits (rule arith-overflow) @ lens.cue:2:11
